{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/322153-roles-are-up-open-dev","id":322153,"title":"Roles Are Up (Open Dev)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-25T14:04:11-08:00","id":322153,"title":"Roles Are Up (Open Dev)","content":"Article <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/playing-at-humanity-roles-promethean-the-created\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> Seems that they are mandatory, have a structure like Mask &amp; Dirge archetypes. 3 sample Aurum Roles. Hint at ways they interact with Breaking Points, as do they the use of supernatural powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T16:23:12-08:00","id":322257,"title":"","content":"It sounds as if the Karma Meter is straight up a scale of Pilgrimage progress, rather than Humanity's more relatively indirect scale of it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T17:48:03-08:00","id":322283,"title":"","content":"Hmm\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2022 So now every Promethean who wants to Redeem must have spent some time in each of the ten Refinements, mastering one of its Roles? Including the likes of Argentum and Plumbum? I\u2019m not sure how I feel about that. Or is it that each Promethean\u2019s Pilgrimage selects, say, half a dozen Refinements that that particular Created must spend time in before he can Redeem? <br /> \u2022 Would the Argentum Roles correspond to the various supernatural templates? E.g., a vampire Role, a werewolf Role, a mage Role, etc.? <br /> \u2022 I\u2019m beginning to see the reason for splitting the Refinements into basic and advanced: the likes of Aes and Mercurius, while useful things to explore, don\u2019t strike me as being as essential to understanding human nature as the likes of Aurum, Stannum, and Ferrum are. It\u2019s almost as if \u201cbasic\u201d and \u201cadvanced\u201d might really mean \u201ccore curriculum\u201d and \u201celectives\u201d, to borrow some terminology from academia. <br /> \u2022 Might the Karma Meter be something like\u201cProgress\u201d? <br /> <br /> Overall, I\u2019m beginning to think that I\u2019d like to see a blog post on just what the Pilgrimage <i>is</i> in 2e; it appears to be much more structured than its 1e counterpart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T18:54:22-08:00","id":322329,"title":"","content":"So, so long as a Promethean rigidly sticks to an archetype, they stop extruding the thing that makes people want to kill them? I'm... Surprisingly ambient about this...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T19:00:09-08:00","id":322334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/322153-roles-are-up-open-dev?p=322283#post322283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 So now every Promethean who wants to Redeem must have spent some time in each of the ten Refinements, mastering one of its Roles? Including the likes of Argentum and Plumbum? I\u2019m not sure how I feel about that. Or is it that each Promethean\u2019s Pilgrimage selects, say, half a dozen Refinements that that particular Created must spend time in before he can Redeem?</div> </div> </div> </div>My impression geared me towards the latter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/322153-roles-are-up-open-dev?p=322283#post322283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 Would the Argentum Roles correspond to the various supernatural templates? E.g., a vampire Role, a werewolf Role, a mage Role, etc.?</div> </div> </div> </div>Holy moly, I hope so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/322153-roles-are-up-open-dev?p=322283#post322283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 Might the Karma Meter be something like\u201cProgress\u201d?<br /> Overall, I\u2019m beginning to think that I\u2019d like to see a blog post on just what the Pilgrimage <i>is</i> in 2e; it appears to be much more structured than its 1e counterpart.</div> </div> </div> </div>Promethean 1e was still very much about the Pilgrimage but it seems to be <i>even more</i> about it in the new edition, so I wouldn't be surprised to learn it gets a bit more mechanical structure. The simple existence of Azothic Memory in the game now is the representation of that theme's changed foundation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T19:00:33-08:00","id":322335,"title":"","content":"I seriously hope that the Integrity/Humanity replacement is <i>not</i> &quot;Progress&quot;, or &quot;Pilgrimage: the Actual Realized Trait, or, Ten Easy Steps to the Golden Dawn!&quot; I would enjoy a bit more structure to the Pilgrimage, but I really do enjoy the vast playground afforded by the ambiguities of 1E. I'm open to more tools and options for players and Storytellers to explore the Pilgrimage, but finding out what Humanity is and how to join it is something that belongs in the space between mechanics and narrative, and not within the tight confines of say, the Follower Role of the Aurum Refinement while Not Being In Charge.<br /> <br /> I'm awaiting more information before being more unsettled by the direction the core conceit of the game is taking. Why is it I love how Mage and Werewolf are shaping up, but Promethean getting a revision feels like I've taken my dog to the vet for a cough, and they just want to keep running tests?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T19:31:15-08:00","id":322351,"title":"","content":"Assuming 3 Roles per Refinement, 1 Milestone per Role, and 10 Milestones for New Dawn, that's a minimum of 4 Refinements.<br /> <br /> And none of those assumptions are actually claims made in the post.<br /> <br /> I think 4 Refinements is a good minimum. I'm guessing... Stannum, 2 Basic Refinements, and 1 Complex Refinement as the default for a very fast Pilgrimage; that doesn't feel too forced, and larger variety and longer distance is probably far more average.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T19:33:01-08:00","id":322352,"title":"","content":"Verge, quick clarification:<br /> <br /> Are you objecting to Progress as the karma meter, or to a stronger structure to the Pilgrimage? I kinda see both objections in your comment but you're implying a connection between them that I can't see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T20:12:21-08:00","id":322374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/322153-roles-are-up-open-dev?p=322283#post322283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2022 So now every Promethean who wants to Redeem must have spent some time in each of the ten Refinements, mastering one of its Roles? Including the likes of Argentum and Plumbum? I\u2019m not sure how I feel about that. Or is it that each Promethean\u2019s Pilgrimage selects, say, half a dozen Refinements that that particular Created must spend time in before he can Redeem?</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems incredibly straightforwardly read as &quot;each Refinement the Promethean follows on his Pilgrimage must have a Role mastered in order to be completed.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T20:14:54-08:00","id":322375,"title":"","content":"Shout-out to the nonbinary pronouns. PtC 2e looks to be a very queer game, and I'm loving it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T20:32:16-08:00","id":322384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/322153-roles-are-up-open-dev?p=322335#post322335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I seriously hope that the Integrity/Humanity replacement is <i>not</i> &quot;Progress&quot;, or &quot;Pilgrimage: the Actual Realized Trait, or, Ten Easy Steps to the Golden Dawn!&quot; I would enjoy a bit more structure to the Pilgrimage, but I really do enjoy the vast playground afforded by the ambiguities of 1E. I'm open to more tools and options for players and Storytellers to explore the Pilgrimage, but finding out what Humanity is and how to join it is something that belongs in the space between mechanics and narrative, and not within the tight confines of say, the Follower Role of the Aurum Refinement while Not Being In Charge.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, 1e\u2019s Humanity was very much that: the closer Humanity got to 10, the closer you were to the New Dawn. Mind you, there were other requirements that had to be met first (e.g., resolving your Milestones and successfully completing the generative act); but once those were accomplished, your Humanity was <i>the</i> determining factor as to whether or not you\u2019d achieve Mortality. I\u2019m very curious as to what 2e\u2019s Karma Meter will be, and hope it will be spoiled soon; but I don\u2019t think that it beng some sort of \u201cprogress meter\u201d is a bad thing, s long as they don\u2019t make the blunder of sayg \u201cwhen you reach 10 on the progress meter, you become human; ntil then, you\u2019re stuck as a Promeihean.\u201d<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/322153-roles-are-up-open-dev?p=322335#post322335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm awaiting more information before being more unsettled by the direction the core conceit of the game is taking. Why is it I love how Mage and Werewolf are shaping up, but Promethean getting a revision feels like I've taken my dog to the vet for a cough, and they just want to keep running tests?</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, I\u2019ve been getting a similar sense. I suspect it\u2019s because we haven\u2019t been getting much in the way of \u201cforest posts\u201d (as in the \u201cforest and trees\u201d saying) \u2014 hardly any posts addressing big picture issues, with nearly every post focusing on this mechanic or that set of splats. For instance, the Refinements: we got two posts about Refinements, one about Basic Refinements and one about Advanced Refinements; but each was basically a list of five Refinements with a capsule summary of each one. Nothing about what these five Refinements have in common that makes them Basic Refinements. The one post that <i>does</i> go \u201cbig picture\u201d was the \u201cbuy in\u201d post, which was presented as a reaction to readers missing the big picture. <br /> <br /> It\u2019s like I\u2019m being told \u201clook; this thing has a trunk!\u201d \u201clook; it has tusks!\u201d \u201clook; it has big, stubby feet!\u201d \u201clook; it has a rope-like tail!\u201d and so on, when what I need are a few more posts along the lines of \u201clook; it\u2019s an elephant!\u201d A bit less about the minutia, and a bit more about the overall design decisions you have in mind. Put a another way, more focus on \u201cwhy are we doing what we\u2019re doing?\u201d instead of the current \u201chere\u2019s what we\u2019re doing\u201d with little to no explanation as to why.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-26-2014, 12:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T20:52:58-08:00","id":322389,"title":"","content":"A thing I feel I should head off before it gets to be pervasive: the phrase is &quot;New Dawn&quot; or &quot;Aurora.&quot; The nearest &quot;Golden Dawn&quot; to Promethean-relevance is a real-world hermetic magical order from the late 19th century. The New Dawn's metaphorical association with the human gold coming from Promethean lead has never had a direct use of the metal's name in any of the published nomenclature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T20:59:22-08:00","id":322390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/322153-roles-are-up-open-dev?p=322375#post322375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shout-out to the nonbinary pronouns. PtC 2e looks to be a very queer game, and I'm loving it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Alchemy <i>does</i> include the concept of the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rebis\" target=\"_blank\">Rebis</a>. That said, I\u2019d prefer that the game keep such things positioned in such a way that those who want to explore such things are free to do so while those who don\u2019t want to don\u2019t feel like they\u2019re being clubbed over the head with it. So far, they\u2019re managing that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T22:19:39-08:00","id":322416,"title":"","content":"So, I get the implication that, in effect, a Promethean who adapts too well to his role essentially grounds the Divine Fire, because they've achieved a pseudo-Humanity by replicating a <i>stereotype </i>of a variety of human.<br /> <br /> I have no objections to this, particularly given how it inevitably fails when the Promethean proves more complex than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T22:31:57-08:00","id":322419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/322153-roles-are-up-open-dev?p=322416#post322416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I get the implication that, in effect, a Promethean who adapts too well to his role essentially grounds the Divine Fire, because they've achieved a pseudo-Humanity by replicating a <i>stereotype </i>of a variety of human.<br /> <br /> I have no objections to this, particularly given how it inevitably fails when the Promethean proves more complex than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Too complex to keep that up forever, not complex enough to be the real thing. Hell of a rock and hard place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T22:50:13-08:00","id":322430,"title":"","content":"That aspect of <b>Promethean</b>\u2019s Roles reminds me of <b>In Nomine</b>\u2019s Roles, which serve a similar function of giving a supernatural being cover from the problems imposed on them by a reality to which they\u2019re not native, but only so long as they stay \u201cin character\u201d and live according to the dictates of their Role.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T23:02:12-08:00","id":322450,"title":"","content":"Dataweaver, re: Humanity - &quot;Progress&quot; implies a certain level of success in the Pilgrimage, rather than sustained success in aping human, for lack of a better term, essentialism. This could be a petty argument, I suppose, but Progress reads as playing the odds: &quot;I have 8 dice in Progress, time to blow this mortal coil!&quot; Humanity says, &quot;I feel like I have this down, maybe now's the time to try...&quot; Or, in another frame, Humanity is an incomplete understanding of the process, that improves one's chances, while Progress implies a dry sort of imminence that undercuts that the Pilgrimage is a fumbling toward Bethlehem. Just because there are milestones doesn't mean the journey's of a finite length. I don't think &quot;Progress&quot; is the term we'll see, but if it's Pilgrimage, Hajj, or Almost There, and how well you do in toeing the line is what gets you there, I will be rolling to resist the Suffocating Rise of Torment.<br /> <br /> Errol216 - Karma Meter, primarily. See above. Dots on a track does not a narrative make. We actually have a pretty decent structure for the Pilgrimage in 1E already, but there is a chasm between Milestones and character apprehension of Milestones. I <i>get </i>Roles as a means to put Milestones above the table, but what's shown here is what I'll call the get human quick scheme: follow this Role for &quot;superlative Milestones&quot;. It's <i>required</i> of all characters, save Freaks, which means it's also the means by which the Pilgrimage is enforced. That's a radical shift from the 1E, free-form structure, which had few actual thresholds or penalties. For some, I know, that's a recipe for wallowing, but I also regard that as a lack of imagination. Besides, wallowing is a part of Promethean experience. What I would like to see is the undeveloped space between a seeking Promethean and a realized Milestone, in a narrative form, rather than a structured Role as part of a karma meter progression. There's also the idea of alchemical narrative, which easily has a place in Promethean's defining arc.<br /> <br /> Dataweaver, re: the same sense - Def. I need a wide angle here. I know what I love about the game and what I hate, and I want to know that the vision still works for me. Blood &amp; Smoke was a departure, but the Requiem didn't change. Vampires are still dirty, sexy predators looking to get a leg up and teeth in. What I get so far from these updates is that Prometheans are randomly made automatons running calculations until they achieve a terminal value of Vitriol, because they were programmed to by Azothic Memory, and will do so until they finally break down or run the program to completion and return a value of $human. That's a far cry from the tragic misbegotten wretches eking out an existence and searching for a place in a hostile world.<br /> <br /> I know I'm not being fair to people I'm grateful to for standing up for my favorite game, but Promethean is one of those rare few things that enchants me, and I am fiercely protective because of that. It's probably for the best that all Dansky ever &quot;leaks&quot; is playlists for Wraith20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T23:03:49-08:00","id":322452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/322153-roles-are-up-open-dev?p=322390#post322390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Alchemy <i>does</i> include the concept of the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rebis\" target=\"_blank\">Rebis</a>. That said, I\u2019d prefer that the game keep such things positioned in such a way that those who want to explore such things are free to do so while those who don\u2019t want to don\u2019t feel like they\u2019re being clubbed over the head with it. So far, they\u2019re managing that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was sort of hoping that they would have a Ferrum Role revolving around gender or racial norms, but there's no way that works out well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T23:24:16-08:00","id":322455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/322153-roles-are-up-open-dev?p=322450#post322450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I get so far from these updates is that Prometheans are randomly made automatons running calculations until they achieve a terminal value of Vitriol, because they were programmed to by Azothic Memory, and will do so until they finally break down or run the program to completion and return a value of $human. That's a far cry from the tragic misbegotten wretches eking out an existence and searching for a place in a hostile world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being that what you get so far from these updates both matches my fundamental no-frills grok of the 1e Pilgrimage by about eighty percent (i.e. you're wandering around in search of experiences that will <i>inscribe the pattern of a soul onto you</i> as the path of least resistance for fixing your particularly volatile mutability-leak) and has <i>absolutely nothing </i>in common with what I've taken from the updates vis-a-vis what's changed, I ask that you keep the hell off of talking about how pissy you're going to be, seeing as such talk makes my soul corrode to countenance in addition to being kind of shitty behavior for a public forum in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T23:25:04-08:00","id":322456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/322153-roles-are-up-open-dev?p=322450#post322450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I get so far from these updates is that Prometheans are randomly made automatons running calculations until they achieve a terminal value of Vitriol, because they were programmed to by Azothic Memory, and will do so until they finally break down or run the program to completion and return a value of $human. That's a far cry from the tragic misbegotten wretches eking out an existence and searching for a place in a hostile world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not so sure that's a fair reading.<br /> <br /> I'm also not so sure that the existence of mechanical support necessarily leads to a situation where it isn't about the narrative... just because you have rules as a support structure doesn't mean that all of the implications that exist for the players exist for the *characters*. The ST having a more defined sense of what the shape of a character's Pilgrimage looks like doesn't mean that the character isn't cluelessly stumbling around, drawing in what bits of wisdom and understanding of their condition that they can... it just means the ST has more guidance for crafting a character arc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T23:28:52-08:00","id":322458,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m pretty sure the Roles are meant to be representative, not comprehensive; so if you want \u201cgender norm\u201d Ferrum Roles and they\u2019re not in the book, it should be easy enough to make them yourself. That said, gender-based Roles would be fine by me: in addition to them being something that you\u2019d only use if you want to, those who aren\u2019t interested in \u201cnon-binary\u201d portrayals could have a male Promethean spend some time perfecting the \u201cmale\u201d Role or a female Promethean perfecting the \u201cfemale\u201d Role while someone who <i>is</i> interested in such things could \u201cplay against type\u201d or have a single Promethean attempt to master both; it\u2019s all in how the gaming group chooses to utilize said Roles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T23:32:33-08:00","id":322461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eolirin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/322153-roles-are-up-open-dev?p=322456#post322456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also not so sure that the existence of mechanical support necessarily leads to a situation where it isn't about the narrative... just because you have rules as a support structure doesn't mean that all of the implications that exist for the players exist for the *characters*. The ST having a more defined sense of what the shape of a character's Pilgrimage looks like doesn't mean that the character isn't cluelessly stumbling around, drawing in what bits of wisdom and understanding of their condition that they can... it just means the ST has more guidance for crafting a character arc.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also, weirdly enough, lends a bit more of a sense as to how elaborate and poetic terminology for a bunch of larval proto-humans' attempts to reach maturity managed to come into common parlance by painting a picture of the Pilgrimage as having a bit more in-universe codification, which seems like a good hook back to things like coded &quot;alchemical texts&quot; written by Prometheans and that little tidbit from the 1e corebook's into to the Refinements about the Promethean organ mortals like Paracelsus made with the development of alchemy.<br /> <br /> That kind of stuff is important so that the game isn't <i>just</i> &quot;wander around engaging the plot for epiphany tokens&quot; - a certain degree of anxiety over whether one has missed a step or done things out of order isn't out of place for the concept, but it's easier to bring that in with a stronger sense of there <i>being</i> a set of steps, however loosely developed, within something like common knowledge among the Created.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-26-2014, 02:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T00:48:30-08:00","id":322488,"title":"","content":"Oddly, Verge, your reading reflects very well Dataweaver's point about not having very many &quot;forest&quot; spoilers. A focus on &quot;tree&quot; spoilers would pretty likely make things seem a lot more mechanistic.<br /> <br /> Near as I've been able to tell from Matt's statements, the design goal of Promethean 2e is to make the game more playable. It's hard to see how he's doing that across all the posts, though, since we can't see most of the glue.<br /> <br /> Actually, now that I think about it, Roles feel like very large Aspirations rather than Virtue/Vices. They're systematically the same tool: a way to convey to the ST what kinds of problems you want to face. There's no mechanical advantage to taking Leader rather than Companion, after all: you're still following Aurum either way: but in picking the Role, you tell the ST you want to figure out the nature of leadership rather than of companionship. Whereas, excepting extraordinary circumstances, your Virtue/Vice follows your character forever, your Role and your Aspirations naturally shift over the character's lifetime. I can see the Role simply replacing the long-term Aspiration suggested in GMC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T01:55:14-08:00","id":322500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/322153-roles-are-up-open-dev?p=322488#post322488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I can see the Role simply replacing the long-term Aspiration suggested in GMC.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or being variant for werewolves Totem Aspirations and mages Obsessions - splat &quot;special&quot; Aspiration.<br /> <br /> But for this I was hoping you will choose <b>yourself</b> a Milestones you want to achieve... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Like, on char sheet you got Conditions section, Aspiration section and Milestones section ( where in <b>Werewolf</b> you got Totem and in <b>Mage</b> you got Obsessions sections ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T02:55:41-08:00","id":322553,"title":"","content":"Maybe you do. It doesn't have to be one or the other, now has it? We haven't taken a look at Milestones yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T10:13:01-08:00","id":322944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/322153-roles-are-up-open-dev?p=322500#post322500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or being variant for werewolves Totem Aspirations and mages Obsessions - splat &quot;special&quot; Aspiration.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find that less likely because Aspirations are heavy. DaveB has said that 3 Aspirations + 3 Obsessions felt like too much in playtesting, and other people have pegged 3 to be an ideal number. The Totem works better, I suspect, because it's a separate entity <i>anyways</i>. I haven't heard anyone actually solve the problem of having too many Aspiration-type things for Mage yet.<br /> <br /> Plus, unlike Mages and Werewolves, it actually makes a lot of sense for Prometheans to have fewer Aspirations that are really theirs and one that is aping the humanity they're trying to understand. With a Mage, they're still human and have human Aspirations, so it doesn't make a whole lot of sense to replace them. A Promethean isn't human and never was.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/322153-roles-are-up-open-dev?p=322500#post322500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But for this I was hoping you will choose <b>yourself</b> a Milestones you want to achieve... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It still makes sense to have the ST pick your Milestones for you, but mechanical communication helps a great deal. Granted, with Roles, you open the door for a passive-aggressive ST who doesn't like your Role, picks an easy and quickly achieved Milestone, then crosses his arms while intimating that you're about to Wasteland the area. But, you know, that's a people problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":2758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","user":"Errol216","date":". 11-26-2014, 01:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T12:06:51-08:00","id":323035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/322153-roles-are-up-open-dev?p=322944#post322944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find that less likely because Aspirations are heavy. DaveB has said that 3 Aspirations + 3 Obsessions felt like too much in playtesting, and other people have pegged 3 to be an ideal number. The Totem works better, I suspect, because it's a separate entity <i>anyways</i>. I haven't heard anyone actually solve the problem of having too many Aspiration-type things for Mage yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>After one year of running <b>Mage</b> on Stop Gap rules, I have - <b>let them have 3 Aspirations + 3 Obsessions</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Sometimes my player were having 2 Aspirations and 1 Obsession. Other times they had full 3 Asp + 3 Obs - and it was good, as this is <i>bonus</i> to game, not main XP generation tool. Also, helped were cabal members shared their common Aspirations or Obsessions - it made them <i>felt</i> like cabal and not a <i>group of random mages working together</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/322153-roles-are-up-open-dev?p=322944#post322944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, unlike Mages and Werewolves, it actually makes a lot of sense for Prometheans to have fewer Aspirations that are really theirs and one that is aping the humanity they're trying to understand. With a Mage, they're still human and have human Aspirations, so it doesn't make a whole lot of sense to replace them. A Promethean isn't human and never was.<br /> <br /> It still makes sense to have the ST pick your Milestones for you, but mechanical communication helps a great deal. Granted, with Roles, you open the door for a passive-aggressive ST who doesn't like your Role, picks an easy and quickly achieved Milestone, then crosses his arms while intimating that you're about to Wasteland the area. But, you know, that's a people problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I'm weird ( or rather <i>wyrd</i> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) but as a player I would like to pick up <i>some</i> of Milestones myself. And best it would be to write them on the sheet. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-26-2014, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T14:25:50-08:00","id":323171,"title":"","content":"Aspirations are a little ambiguous because GMC and Blood and Smoke (sorry, Requiem 2e, now) present them slightly differently, but I'm of the opinion that the GMC note that Aspirations don't *need* to be in character holds for all lines. So Prometheans not being human to begin with wouldn't mean anything to the Aspiration system. It's value as a flag to draw attention to things that the *player* wants to have happen is too important of a signaling tool to do away with (or minimize) in favor of a single overriding Role.<br /> <br /> Also, as to choosing Milestones, I don't know that there needs to be any explicit support for that, as how much say a player has in that selection is more of a social contract thing with the ST. Individual groups need to find their own comfort levels in terms of how much of the character arc is ST driven and how much is player driven, as there's no easy universal balance to that kind of thing. If you want say in some of your milestones, you should talk to your ST about it and work something out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":614,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","user":"Eolirin","date":". 11-26-2014, 05:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T14:30:06-08:00","id":323176,"title":"","content":"Just to reiterate Thorbes point before it gets lost in speculation:<br /> <br /> We have not yet seen Milestones and how they have changed in 2E Promethean. We've seen Roles and how they add a Milestone to the character. That it. How Milestones are selected and implemented remains to be seen.<br /> <br /> Please keep this in mind before going off on wild speculation about the whole Aspiration System getting overhauled for Promethean 2E and Milestones being decided by the ST from a sample list or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T07:22:01-08:00","id":323616,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Whatever the case, turning his back on his Role means ignoring the milestone in front of him. This is not in and of itself a problem, but <b>if the Role is related to his Pilgrimage</b>, it gives him a real chance of stepping back along his Pilgrimage.</span></span> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> Just wanted to chime in trying to highlight a point that seems strange to me as of now. I thought Prometheans needed to explore all Refinements, so how can a specific Role be related to the Pilgrimage if all Refinements must be accomplished?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T11:33:30-08:00","id":323781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/322153-roles-are-up-open-dev?p=323616#post323616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just wanted to chime in trying to highlight a point that seems strange to me as of now. I thought Prometheans needed to explore all Refinements, so how can a specific Role be related to the Pilgrimage if all Refinements must be accomplished?</div> </div> </div> </div>AFAIK, there is nothing that states that a Promethean is required to sample every Refinement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T20:04:56-08:00","id":324160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">A Promethean must master at least one Role in each of the Refinements on his Pilgrimage</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>5th line of the Roles article. But again, &quot;on his pilgrimage&quot; is appearing....what could this mean?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T20:09:15-08:00","id":324163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/322153-roles-are-up-open-dev?p=324160#post324160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 5th line of the Roles article. But again, &quot;on his pilgrimage&quot; is appearing....what could this mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;That he adheres to, ever.&quot;<br /> <br /> This is not a deep mystery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T20:26:48-08:00","id":324169,"title":"","content":"Err\u2026 \u201cIf the Role is related to his Pilgrimage\u201d implies that some Roles that a Promethean pursues <i>aren\u2019t</i> related to his Pilgrimage. It\u2019s not necessarily as cut and dry as you\u2019re saying, Satchel; even in 1e, we had the whole \u201cStoryteller determines your Milestones\u201d thing. Consider the Imperium Appendix in <b>Imperial Mysteries</b>, with its Noumenon and Omens \u2014 and the box about \u201cProfane Omens\u201d(?), which are essentially acts of Imperium that aren\u2019t part of the Golden Road Ascension. P2e might be doing something similar, with a Pilgrimage \u201cchecklist\u201d of Roles that you must master to achieve your New Dawn (the general nature of which gets established at the start of the Pilgrimage) and with other Roles essentially serving as detours that don\u2019t get you any closer to the Aurora.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not particularly <i>in favor</i> of such an approach, mind you; especially if the Storyteller determines what the make of the Pilgrimage is. But it is distinctly possible tuat this is exactly what P2e is going to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-27-2014, 11:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T20:38:47-08:00","id":324192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/322153-roles-are-up-open-dev?p=324169#post324169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Err\u2026 \u201cIf the Role is related to his Pilgrimage\u201d implies that some Roles that a Promethean pursues <i>aren\u2019t</i> related to his Pilgrimage.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are multiple Roles in each Refinement. The only &quot;Refinement&quot; that isn't related to the Pilgrimage is Flux, and the only unambiguous requirement in the post is that completing the Pilgrimage necessitates mastering roles from different Refinements.<br /> <br /> The quotation you're pulling is from the section that talks about a behavior that is <i>not </i>conducive to mastering a Role; the very next paragraph fairly transparently indicates that Roles are a consciously pursued thing as part of the Created attempting to reach the New Dawn in some manner of self-defined state.<br /> <br /> If you're aiming to become a human for which &quot;Companion&quot; is a useful facet of description, turning your back on the Role of Companion is obviously not a step forward. Learning about being a Leader could still fulfill the basic internalization requirements, but the lessons of Leaders are not the same as the lessons of Companions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-27-2014, 11:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T06:21:47-08:00","id":324445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/322153-roles-are-up-open-dev?p=323035#post323035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to pick up <i>some</i> of Milestones myself. And best it would be to write them on the sheet. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect part of the point of Roles is to split the difference. You might (or might not) be picking the specific form the milestone takes, but you're likely to be picking your Roles, and thus indicating the <i>sort</i> of thing you want the milestone to be.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}